### 2.4 Failure Modes & Mitigations (Hardened)

- **Unauthorized growth** → Absolute frequency lock + physical key. System refuses any expansion without both.  
- **Uncontrolled deposition** → Geometry-enforced electrode lattice + energy limiting. Growth stops the instant the covenant fails.  
- **Particulate depletion during expansion** → Continuous reserve feed + real-time “material remaining” estimate. Refuses growth if reserve < 25% without override.  
- **Contamination of purification stream** → Automatic isolation valves + full system lockout until manual reset by ultimate user.  
- **Power loss** → Graceful degradation: existing lattice remains structural; purification continues on residual charge for 30–90 minutes; expansion aborts cleanly.

